    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now the most useful identity in the chapter:\n\na^2 − b^2 = (a + b)(a − b)\n\n105^2 − 95^2\n= (105 + 95)(105 − 95)\n= 200 × 10\n= 2000\n\nTwo hard multiplications became one easy one.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The book uses this on monsters like:\n\n75983 × 75983 − 45983 × 45983\n= (75983 + 45983)(75983 − 45983)\n= 121966 × 30000\n\nNobody wants to square 75983 directly. The identity exists so you never have to.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
