    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Subtract the identities instead, and the squares cancel:\n\n(a + b)^2 − (a − b)^2 = 4ab\n\nTry a = 9, b = 2:\n\n11^2 − 7^2 = 121 − 49 = 72\n4 × 9 × 2 = 72 ✓",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So when you see:\n\n(a + b)^2 − (a − b)^2\n\nyou only need the product: 4 × a × b.\n\nSame shape family, different survivor: sum kills 2ab, difference kills the squares.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5"
        }
      ]
    },
