    "teach_7": {
      "id": "teach_7",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "One more backwards run, straight from the book:\n\na^2 + b^2 = 117 and ab = 54. Find (a + b)/(a − b).\n\nBuild each piece:\n\n(a + b)^2 = 117 + 2 × 54 = 225 → a + b = 15\n(a − b)^2 = 117 − 2 × 54 = 9 → a − b = 3",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_7_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_7_step": {
      "id": "teach_7_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now the ratio:\n\n(a + b)/(a − b) = 15/3 = 5\n\nNotice: the identity gave a + b and a − b separately, and the question only needed their ratio.\n\nRead the question before solving more than necessary.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_7"
        }
      ]
    },
